{"about_the_game":"<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Story:</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The evil space pirate Krater has dispatched his robotic army to capture all of the planets in the system.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The only hope to stop him is Comit the Astrodian, a meteor man from the planet Astrodia who has a rocket pack attached to his back.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Kick Krater off each planet and take back the system.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Comit's Abilities:</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Comit can use his rocket pack to boost and double jump his way through each stage while collecting yellow and red stars that give him lives or</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >allow him to entire bonus stages.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Development:</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Comit is designed like early 90's platformers because it was actually created back then on paper. The first prototype was created in 2011. The current</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >incarnation started development in January of 2016. While simple in formula, the game was created to hold true to it's original 1994 blueprint with the </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >addition of a save system that was created to accommodate the modern style of game.</p>","achievements":{"total":0},"background":"https://store.akamai.steamstatic.com/images/storepagebackground/app/546790?t=1726981754","background_raw":"https://store.akamai.steamstatic.com/images/storepagebackground/app/546790?t=1726981754","capsule_image":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/546790/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1726981754","capsule_imagev5":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/546790/capsule_184x69.jpg?t=1726981754","categories":[{"description":"Single-player","id":2},{"description":"Steam Achievements","id":22},{"description":"Full controller support","id":28},{"description":"Steam Trading Cards","id":29},{"description":"Family Sharing","id":62}],"content_descriptors":{"ids":[],"notes":null},"controller_support":"full","detailed_description":"<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Story:</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The evil space pirate Krater has dispatched his robotic army to capture all of the planets in the system.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The only hope to stop him is Comit the Astrodian, a meteor man from the planet Astrodia who has a rocket pack attached to his back.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Kick Krater off each planet and take back the system.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Comit's Abilities:</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Comit can use his rocket pack to boost and double jump his way through each stage while collecting yellow and red stars that give him lives or</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >allow him to entire bonus stages.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Development:</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Comit is designed like early 90's platformers because it was actually created back then on paper. The first prototype was created in 2011. The current</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >incarnation started development in January of 2016. While simple in formula, the game was created to hold true to it's original 1994 blueprint with the </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >addition of a save system that was created to accommodate the modern style of game.</p>","developers":["LunarCore Games"],"genres":[{"description":"Action","id":"1"},{"description":"Indie","id":"23"}],"header_image":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/546790/header.jpg?t=1726981754","is_free":false,"legal_notice":"\u00a92016-2022 LunarCore Games